    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0369" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 406/69–71.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Collier</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 145.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the protection of United States and Spanish trade-marks in China, I
                    inclose copy of a dispatch<anchor n="a" xml:id="d214-f1"/> from the American
                    minister at Peking reporting <pb facs="0370" n="258" xml:id="pg258"/> that the
                    Spanish minister at that place does not regard himself as able to effect the
                    agreement by exchange of notes unless he receives specific instructions in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>The department hopes that the instructions referred to will be given.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
